<p>No I&amp;B thread. No Draft thread. Make <em>sure</em> you read and follow the articles linked in step one (listed below):</p>
<hr />
<p>Typically, cold-posted articles don't survive very long. For the best chances of having an article that survives the mainlist, follow these steps:</p>
<ol>
<li>Give the following pages a read: <a href="/guide-for-newbies">Guide for Newbies</a> and <a href="/how-to-write-an-scp">How To Write an SCP</a>.</li>
<li>Copy the source of your cold-posted article into your own <a href="http://scp-sandbox-3.wikidot.com/">Sandbox page</a> (instructions for setting up your sandbox page on frontpage of sandbox).</li>
<li>Write up a brief summary of your concept in the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-and-brainstorming">Ideas and Brainstorming forum</a> and get critiques on your concept.</li>
<li>Once the concept is sufficiently critiqued, start drafting! When you get to a good enough point to where it can be critiqued, toss a link to your sandbox page in the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/c-50864/help:drafts-and-critiques">Drafts and Critiques forum</a> for crits on your draft.</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<p>That said, this isn't a <em>bad</em> idea. It just needs quite a bit of refining, as to the points mentioned above.</p>

