<p>Well, if this gets deleted, be sure to have copied the source of your article into your sandbox. Keep in mind, friend, that the mainlist is a place for summary judgement of finished works.</p>
<p>Honestly, the whole process should be done within the Wiki and Sandbox because <em>this</em> is your audience. We have the I&amp;B board so that an idea can be refined <em>before</em> drafting, and during/after drafting, we have the D&amp;C to help refine the article.</p>
<p>Throughout those steps, there is also the <em>immensely</em> helpful <a href="http://05command.wikidot.com/forum-crit-main">Forum Crit Team</a> who are, mostly, available on the IRC chatroom (location: #thecritters) or who accept private messages.</p>
<p>So, with all that said, your idea is actually quite an interesting one, but it can be taken further. However, if it gets deleted, send me a Private Message, and I'd be willing to give some pointers on how to tone it up conceptually and, hopefully, give you the overall direction you're looking for.</p>
<hr />
<p>Personal note here &#8212; never hold so tightly to an idea that you close off the idea of its transformation. You may be closing it off to the best and brightest writers on the `net. Almost <em>all</em> works here on the wiki are, in one form or another, products of collaboration.</p>

