			<div class="content" id="post-content-4121970">
									

<p>I got an idea&#8230;</p>
<p>&quot;The SCP seems to have a strange aura surrounding it, measuring approximately 5 meters. Anyone who enters said aura claims to feel an extreme pressure to 'ask for a toy' from SCP-4118. This aura is created by unkown methods, possibly a new form of radiation, and shall be investigated further.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Any and all attempts to destroy instances of SCP-4118-1 result in failure, and are met with hostility towards staff. However, all SCP-4118-1s attempts of harming staff result in minor punctures and scratches due to their small nature.&quot;</p>
<p>If you can make it seem strange like that, without explaining it in too much detail, then this could be a great SCP. You definitely have my permission to take those quotes, btw. Just make sure that all details you add explain only what's needed, any more and it seems like a comic instead of an SCP. Make us feel like the scientists, make us want to know more, you definitely are capable of it.</p>
<p>Adding detail to a story is a great thing, don't get me wrong, but adding too much makes it easier to get the idea, thus turning people away. If people don't completely understand what it is they are looking at, but know the idea, they will read more to find out.</p>

							</div>

								
					
